@*
    The _PageForm composer's client-side scripts (rich editor + grant-picker
    sync + the ADR 0041 visibility-block toggling).

    Kept in its OWN partial (not inside _PageForm.cshtml) because a `@section`
    declared in a partial is a known Razor gotcha: the section is not reliably
    registered with the layout's `RenderSectionAsync`, so the whole block
    (including the `change` listener that reveals #page-individual-block) can
    be silently dropped. The two consuming views (New.cshtml / Edit.cshtml)
    declare `@section Scripts` in the VIEW file and include this partial —
    matching every other view in the app (Login, Signup, Posts, Profile,
    Groups all declare their `@section` in the view, never in a partial).
*@
<script type="module" src="~/js/lib/rich-editor.js"></script>
@* TG U8 — the composer tag-input autocomplete (client/lib/tag-suggest.ts,
   tsc-built, no editor dependency — the RE·3 idiom). Self-wires any
   input[data-tag-suggest]; on a `PageKind.User` blog page that is the Tags
   field the _PageForm renders (the `System`-page composer renders **no**
   input, C-TG·6 — the module self-wire finds nothing and is a no-op there).
   The filter + ≤ 10 cap are server-side via POST /api/tags/suggest
   (the SuggestAsync seam, C-TG·2 / C-TG·4). *@
<script type="module" src="~/js/lib/tag-suggest.js"></script>
